  "id": "BIT-kyverno-2026-122302",
  "summary": "Kyverno before 1.19.2 Privilege Escalation via Generate Rule Permission Check",
  "details": "Kyverno before 1.19.2 contains a privilege escalation vulnerability that allows namespace admins to create resources beyond their RBAC because generate-rule admission checks verify the controller's permissions, not the author's. Attackers can create a namespaced Policy with generate rules targeting other namespaces or cluster-scoped kinds, making the background controller create or clone resources cluster-wide.",
